---
title: Pulled Pork
servings: 6
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 3 hours
source: https://www.recipetineats.com/pork-carnitas-mexican-slow-cooker-pulled-pork/
tags:
  - dinner
  - meat
  - pork
  - bbq
  - long
  - medium
---

Pat dry @pork shoulder{550%g} and trim excess fat. Season generously with @salt{} and @black pepper{}.

Heat #pot{} over medium-high heat. Add @canola oil{3%tbsp} and sear the pork on all sides until well browned. Remove and set aside.

Reduce heat to medium-low. Add thinly sliced @onion{1%large} and cook for ~{5%minutes} until softened.

Add crushed @garlic{4%cloves} and cook for another ~{1%minute} until fragrant.

Add @ketchup{0.33%cup}, @apple cider vinegar{2%tbsp}, @Dijon mustard{1%tbsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp}, @brown sugar{1.5%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1%tsp}, @ground cumin{0.125%tsp}, @bay leaves{2} and @water{1%cup}. Stir and bring to a boil.

Return the pork to the pot along with any accumulated juices. Add enough @water{} to reach halfway up the sides of the pork.

Bring to a boil, flipping the pork to coat in the sauce. Reduce heat to low, cover and simmer for ~{2.5-3%hours}, flipping and basting every 30 minutes. Add more water if the sauce becomes too dry.

Remove the pork and let cool slightly. Shred using two forks.

If the sauce is too thin, boil uncovered until reduced to the desired consistency.

Mix the shredded pork with some of the BBQ sauce before serving. Serve with extra sauce, coleslaw and toasted burger buns or sandwich bread.
